IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc25-remediation-negotiation`

-- ccc25-tests-remediation-negotiation.l4 -- tests for sections 715.3 to 715.35 (src lines 14875 to 14952).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, with the words that decide it. A JUST FALSE is expected only where the text says no in its own words;
-- a NOTHING is expected where the text does not answer, including a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails (the coordinator ruling 2026-11-12).

§ `Section 715.3(1) -- definitions`
-- 14875: court means a superior court of criminal jurisdiction but does not include a court of appeal.
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) court` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a superior court of criminal jurisdiction, by s 2, and not a court of appeal
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) court` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not include a court of appeal, whatever s 2 says
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) court` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- s 2 says no: the means-definition says no
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) court` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 does not answer, so this is not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) court` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a court of appeal is excluded in the text's own words, even where s 2 does not answer
-- 14876: offence means any offence listed in the schedule to this Part.
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) offence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- means any offence listed: not listed, the text says no
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) offence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- the schedule's answer is outside this range and not covered
-- 14877: organization has the same meaning as in section 2 but does not include a public body, trade union or municipality. Arguments: s 2 answer, public body, trade union, municipality.
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- organization within s 2, none of the three exclusions
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not include a public body
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not include a trade union
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not include a municipality
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- s 2 says it is not an organization
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 does not answer
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) organization` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a public body is excluded in the text's own words, whatever s 2 says
-- 14878: an agreement, between an organization accused of having committed an offence and a prosecutor, to stay any proceedings related to that offence if the organization complies.
-- Arguments: it is an agreement; one party is an organization (this Part's answer); the organization is accused; the offence is an offence (this Part's answer); the other party is a prosecutor; it is to stay proceedings if the organization complies.
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element present
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an agreement
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the organization is not accused
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the other party is not a prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no stay of proceedings if the organization complies
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one party is not an organization of this Part
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the offence is not listed in the schedule
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the organization answer is not covered and nothing else says no
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence answer is not covered and nothing else says no
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` TRUE NOTHING TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one limb is a plain no even though the other is not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) remediation agreement` FALSE NOTHING TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an agreement is a plain no whatever the other answers
-- 14879: victim has the same meaning as in section 2 but, for an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, it includes any person outside Canada. Arguments: s 2 answer, that offence, person outside Canada.
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) victim` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a victim within s 2
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) victim` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- includes any person outside Canada for an offence under section 3 or 4 of that Act
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) victim` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- within Canada the s 2 answer stands: not a victim
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) victim` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- outside Canada but not an offence under section 3 or 4 of that Act: s 2 stands
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) victim` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- includes any person outside Canada: no need for the s 2 answer
#ASSERT `s 715.3(1) victim` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 does not answer and the extension does not apply

§ `Section 715.3(2) -- a third party acting for the victim`
-- 14881: a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may also act on a victim's behalf when authorized to do so by the court, if the victim requests it or the prosecutor deems it appropriate.
-- Arguments: s 2.2 answer for the third party; the court has authorized; the victim requests; the prosecutor deems it appropriate. Not referred to in 2.2 is read as: s 2.2 does not answer JUST TRUE (fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- authorized by the court, and the victim requests it
#ASSERT `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- authorized by the court, and the prosecutor deems it appropriate
#ASSERT `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- s 2.2 says no to this person, so they are not referred to in it; both triggers
#ASSERT `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- authorized but neither trigger: the grant's "if" gate fails, so this is not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- when not authorized by the court the text says no (a "when" gate, listed)
#ASSERT `s 715.3(2) a third party not referred to in section 2.2 may act on the victim’s behalf` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a third party who is referred to in section 2.2 is outside this subsection

§ `Section 715.32 -- conditions for negotiation`
-- 14891-14895 (1): the prosecutor may enter into negotiations ... if the following conditions are met. Arguments: organization answer; alleged to have committed the offence; offence answer; (a) reasonable prospect; (b) no serious harm or injury to national defence or security; (b) not for the benefit of a criminal organization or terrorist group; (c) public interest; (d) AG consent. Paragraph (b) holds two opinions, so the four paragraphs are five inputs.
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every condition met
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) no reasonable prospect of conviction: the "if" gate fails on a grant, not covered (fork F2.2)
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) serious harm: gate fails
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) criminal organization: gate fails
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (c) not in the public interest: gate fails
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (d) no consent of the Attorney General: gate fails
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an organization of this Part: outside the grant's own wording
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a listed offence: outside the grant's own wording
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not alleged to have committed it: outside the grant's own wording
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the organization answer is not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor may enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the offence answer is not covered

-- 14897-14906 (2): the prosecutor must consider the following factors (a) to (i). Argument: the factor; whether the prosecutor considers the factor relevant (read only for paragraph (i)).
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(a) the circumstances in which the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence was brought to the attention of investigative authorities` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (a) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(a) the circumstances in which the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence was brought to the attention of investigative authorities` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (a), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(b) the nature and gravity of the act or omission and its impact on any victim` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (b) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(b) the nature and gravity of the act or omission and its impact on any victim` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (b), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(c) the degree of involvement of senior officers of the organization in the act or omission` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (c) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(c) the degree of involvement of senior officers of the organization in the act or omission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (c), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(d) whether the organization has taken disciplinary action, including termination of employment, against any person who was involved in the act or omission` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (d) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(d) whether the organization has taken disciplinary action, including termination of employment, against any person who was involved in the act or omission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (d), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(e) whether the organization has made reparations or taken other measures to remedy the harm caused by the act or omission and to prevent the commission of similar acts or omissions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (e) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(e) whether the organization has made reparations or taken other measures to remedy the harm caused by the act or omission and to prevent the commission of similar acts or omissions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (e), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(f) whether the organization has identified or expressed a willingness to identify any person involved in wrongdoing related to the act or omission` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (f) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(f) whether the organization has identified or expressed a willingness to identify any person involved in wrongdoing related to the act or omission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (f), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(g) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — was convicted of an offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body, or whether it entered into a previous remediation agreement or other settlement, in Canada or elsewhere, for similar acts or omissions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (g) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(g) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — was convicted of an offence or sanctioned by a regulatory body, or whether it entered into a previous remediation agreement or other settlement, in Canada or elsewhere, for similar acts or omissions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (g), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(h) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — is alleged to have committed any other offences, including those not listed in the schedule to this Part` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (h) is a factor whether or not the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(h) whether the organization — or any of its representatives — is alleged to have committed any other offences, including those not listed in the schedule to this Part` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the listed factor (h), and the prosecutor thinks it relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(i) any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- any other factor the prosecutor considers relevant
#ASSERT `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor must consider the factor` `s 715.32(2)(i) any other factor that the prosecutor considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a factor the prosecutor does not consider relevant: the list is not closed, not covered

-- 14908 (3): despite paragraph (2)(i), if the organization is alleged to have committed an offence under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, the prosecutor must not consider the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved. Arguments: the matter; that offence is alleged.
#ASSERT `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` `s 715.32(3) the national economic interest` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named matter, that offence alleged
#ASSERT `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` `s 715.32(3) the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named matter, that offence alleged
#ASSERT `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` `s 715.32(3) the identity of the organization or individual involved` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named matter, that offence alleged
#ASSERT `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` `s 715.32(3) a matter that none of those names` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other matter: the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor must not consider the matter` `s 715.32(3) the national economic interest` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "if" is the text's own condition: no such offence alleged, the bar does not apply

§ `Section 715.33 -- the notice`
-- 14910 (1): If the prosecutor wishes to negotiate a remediation agreement, they must give the organization written notice.
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the prosecutor must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the prosecutor wishes to negotiate
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the prosecutor must give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty arises only on the text's "If": it does not arise otherwise
-- 14910-14920: the notice must include (a) to (j). Argument order: written notice given to the organization; (a) summary of the offence; (b) voluntary nature; (c) legal effects; (d) waiver of delay; (e) good faith and information; (f) use of information; (g) warning on false statements; (h) withdrawal; (i) victims; (j) deadline to accept.
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- written and every paragraph (a) to (j) present
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: written notice of the offer given to the organization
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (d)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (e)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (f)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (g)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (h)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (i)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(1) the notice meets the requirement that it be written and include each of paragraphs (a) to (j)` (`s 715.33(1) what the notice includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: (j)

-- 14922 (2): no admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility made by the organization during the negotiations is admissible against it in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission, except those contained in the statement of facts or admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs 715.34(1)(a) and (b), if the parties reach an agreement and it is approved by the court.
-- Arguments: an admission, confession or statement; made by the organization during the negotiations; offered against it; contained in the statement of facts or admission; agreement reached and approved.
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an admission made in negotiations, offered against the organization, and the exception is not met
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the exception is met: contained in the statement of facts and the agreement is approved (the text says it is not inadmissible)
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the exception needs approval by the court as well: not approved, the bar stands
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- approved, but not contained in the statement of facts or admission: the bar stands
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made during the negotiations: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.33(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not offered against the organization: outside the subsection

§ `Section 715.34 -- contents of the agreement`
-- 14924-14943 (1): a remediation agreement must include (a) to (p). Field order: (a); (b); (c); (d); (e) identifies property; (e)(i) forfeit to Canada; (e)(ii) forfeit to a province; (e)(iii) otherwise deal; (f); (g) reparations; (g) reasons for none; (g) measure in lieu; (h) surcharge; (h) every offence is under section 3 or 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act; (i) report; (i) manner of report; (j); (k) acknowledgement; (k) commitment; (l); (m); (n); (o); (p).
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every item present; no property identified (nothing to forfeit); reparations given; surcharge given
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (a): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (b): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (c): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (d): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (f): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (i) report: the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (i) manner of reporting: the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (j): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (k) acknowledgement: the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (k) commitment: the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (l): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (m): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (n): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (o): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing (p): the agreement must include it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (e): property identified but no obligation to forfeit or deal with it
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): property identified and the obligation (e)(i) present
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): property identified and the obligation (e)(ii) present
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): property identified and the obligation (e)(iii) present
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): no property identified, so the forfeiture limbs do not matter
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g): no reparations, but a statement of reasons and a measure in lieu
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (g): reasons without a measure in lieu
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (g): a measure in lieu without a statement of reasons
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (g): none of the three
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (h): no surcharge obligation and not every offence is under section 3 or 4 of that Act
#ASSERT `s 715.34(1) the remediation agreement includes everything that it must include` (`s 715.34(1) what the agreement includes` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (h): every offence is under section 3 or 4 of that Act, so no surcharge is required

-- 14945 (2): no admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility made by the organization as a result of the agreement is admissible against it in any civil or criminal proceedings related to that act or omission, except those contained in the statement of facts and admission of responsibility referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b), if the agreement is approved by the court.
-- Arguments: an admission, confession or statement; made as a result of the agreement; offered against the organization; contained in the statement of facts and admission; the agreement is approved.
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- made as a result of the agreement, and the exception is not met
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the exception is met
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the exception needs approval of the agreement
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- approved, but not contained in the statement of facts and admission
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an admission: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made as a result of the agreement: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.34(2) the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the organization` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not offered against the organization: outside the subsection

-- 14947-14950 (3): a remediation agreement may include, among other things, (a) compliance measures; (b) reimbursement of the prosecutor's costs; (c) an independent monitor.
#ASSERT `s 715.34(3) the remediation agreement may include the term` `s 715.34(3)(a) an indication of the obligation for the organization to establish, implement or enhance compliance measures to address any deficiencies in the organization’s policies, standards or procedures — including those related to internal control procedures and employee training — that may have allowed the act or omission` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.34(3) the remediation agreement may include the term` `s 715.34(3)(b) an indication of the obligation for the organization to reimburse the prosecutor for any costs identified in the agreement that are related to its administration and that have or will be incurred by the prosecutor` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.34(3) the remediation agreement may include the term` `s 715.34(3)(c) an indication of the fact that an independent monitor has been appointed, as selected with the prosecutor’s approval, to verify and report to the prosecutor on the organization’s compliance` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.34(3) the remediation agreement may include the term` `s 715.34(3) a term that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- among other things: the list is not closed

§ `Section 715.35 -- the independent monitor`
-- 14952: a candidate for appointment as an independent monitor must notify the prosecutor in writing of any previous or ongoing relationship, in particular with the organization or any of its representatives, that may have a real or perceived impact on the candidate's ability to provide an independent verification. Arguments: a candidate; a relationship; a real or perceived impact.
#ASSERT `s 715.35 the candidate must notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a candidate with such a relationship
#ASSERT `s 715.35 the candidate must notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a candidate: outside the section
#ASSERT `s 715.35 the candidate must notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no relationship: outside the section
#ASSERT `s 715.35 the candidate must notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a relationship with no real or perceived impact on independence: outside the section

§ `Regulative rules of sections 715.32 to 715.35, run with #TRACE`
-- Each trace is expected to end as the comment above it says. No WITHIN is stated in the text for any of them, so an act not done leaves a standing obligation, never a breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the prosecutor may enter into negotiations and does)
#TRACE `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor's permission to enter into negotiations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.32(1) enter into negotiations for a remediation agreement` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (a permission not used stays open)
#TRACE `s 715.32(1) the prosecutor's permission to enter into negotiations` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the prosecutor considers the factors)
#TRACE `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor's duty to consider the factors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.32(2) consider the factors` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.32(2) the prosecutor's duty to consider the factors` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT BREACHED   (the prosecutor considers a barred matter)
#TRACE `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor's prohibition on considering the national economic interest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.32(3) consider the national economic interest, the potential effect on relations with a state other than Canada or the identity of the organization or individual involved` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (the bar stands while nothing barred has been considered)
#TRACE `s 715.32(3) the prosecutor's prohibition on considering the national economic interest` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the prosecutor gives the notice)
#TRACE `s 715.33(1) the prosecutor's duty to give written notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.33(1) give the organization written notice of the offer to enter into negotiations` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.33(1) the prosecutor's duty to give written notice` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the candidate notifies the prosecutor)
#TRACE `s 715.35 the candidate's duty to notify the prosecutor` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 715.35 a candidate for appointment as an independent monitor` DOES `s 715.35 notify the prosecutor in writing of the relationship` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stands)
#TRACE `s 715.35 the candidate's duty to notify the prosecutor` AT 0 WITH

